<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">About the </ansi><ansi fg="command">Waystone Hollow</ansi>

A handful of travellers between roads wait in the Waystone Hollow, a cave
in the bluff west of Scrub Draw, above Pothole Coulee, for someone worth
going with. Each has a corner of the cave to themselves. There is only one
of each of them in the world: while one travels with somebody, nobody else
can have them.

Nobody is handed one. You have to win them over.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Winning one over ━━━</ansi>

Talk to them. Tell them who you are and what you have done. Bring them
things to show (<ansi fg="command">show</ansi> <ansi fg="yellow">item</ansi> <ansi fg="mobname">name</ansi>): something you made, something
you found, proof of something you did. They can see how you look and what
you wear, what you are good at, what you have fought, the tasks you have
seen through and how the people of the world regard you. Each of them cares
about different things, so ask.

They decide for themselves, the way a person would. Try to talk them into
coming with you, if you like, but nobody can sign them on: when one of them
has made up their mind about you, they will ask you themselves whether you
would like their company, and your answer is up to you. None of them will
ask someone who has not yet given them a single reason to think well of
them, or someone they distrust or dislike.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Who they will talk to ━━━</ansi>

On this server the travellers in the Hollow talk only with players who
bring their own key (the web client's Companion key button; see
<ansi fg="command">help aicompanion</ansi>). Without one, they will not
hear you. The board at the cave mouth says what speaking to them sends and
where (<ansi fg="command">look board</ansi>); speaking to one after reading
it is your agreement.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ If it goes wrong ━━━</ansi>

A companion who comes to distrust and dislike you badly enough will leave
you and go back to the Hollow. So will one whose company you send away
(<ansi fg="command">companion-part</ansi>), and one who has waited for you
too long while you were away. They take what they have learned with them,
and leave you what you gave them. You can go back and try to win them, or
another, over again.

